[1m[38;5;231mWhat user data may leave the browser in a log record?[0m

[38;5;153m❯[39m [38;5;246m1.[39m [38;5;153mAllowlist + hashed user id (Recommended)[39m
     [38;5;246mOnly explicitly-safe fields, plus a one-way hash of the username for correlation. No raw identifiers ever stored.[39m
  [38;5;246m2.[39m Strict allowlist, no user id
     [38;5;246mSafe fields and a random session id only. Strongest guarantee; you can't tie a log line to a specific reported [39m
     [38;5;246muser.[39m
  [38;5;246m3.[39m Allowlist + plaintext username
     [38;5;246mEasiest support matching, but stores user identifiers with the vendor and widens your data-protection scope.[39m
